---
/** Home page. Visual design ported from reference/shap-postal-round.html; content per docs/build-brief.md. */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { FACTS, ROUNDS, SITE } from '../lib/config.ts';
---
<Base
  description="Walk or run the old Shap postman's round: a heritage route through Swindale and Wet Sleddale on the eastern edge of the Lake District, starting and finishing at Birchwood Cafe."
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker"><span class="slot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Shap, Cumbria</div>
          <h1>{SITE.name}</h1>
          <p class="strap">{SITE.strapline}</p>
          <p class="lede">
            Until 1976 a postman walked the post out of Shap every morning: over the fields to Shap Abbey, up to isolated
            Tailbert, down into Swindale and over the fell to Wet Sleddale. Now you can walk or run the round yourself.
          </p>
          <p>{SITE.placement}</p>
          <blockquote class="quote">
            It broke my heart.
            <cite>Stuart Lewis, the last postman to walk the round, on being given a van</cite>
          </blockquote>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn" href="/route/">The route</a>
            <a class="btn red" href="/log/">Log your round</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <dl class="facts" aria-label="Route at a glance">
          {
            FACTS.map(([k, v]) => (
              <>
                <dt>{k}</dt>
                <dd>{v}</dd>
              </>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="why-h">
      <div class="wrap book">
        <div class="book-card">
          <strong>Why Birchwood Cafe?</strong>
          The café is run by the family who ran Shap’s post office and sorting office for generations. The post always
          began here, so the round does too.
        </div>
        <div class="measure">
          <h2 id="why-h">Two rounds, one start</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>{ROUNDS.long.name}</strong> is about {ROUNDS.long.miles} miles, the full round as the postie walked
            it. <strong>{ROUNDS.short.name}</strong> is about {ROUNDS.short.miles} miles, leaving out the summer-only
            cottages.
          </p>
          <p>
            It isn’t a race. Walk it or run it, in one go or in stages. If you’d like to, add your name to the round book
            when you’re back.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/story/">Read the story of the round</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="plan-h">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="plan-h">Plan your round</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <a class="card" href="/route/">
            <h3>The route</h3>
            <p>Both rounds, stop by stop, with GPX downloads and current notices.</p>
            <p class="more">See the route →</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="/safety/">
            <h3>Safety &amp; respect</h3>
            <p>Rough, pathless, unwaymarked fell. What to take, and how to look after the land.</p>
            <p class="more">Before you go →</p>
          </a>
          <a class="card" href="/log/">
            <h3>The round book</h3>
            <p>Done it? Log your round with any free GPS app and see who else has.</p>
            <p class="more">Log your round →</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
